{"pageProps":{"story":{"name":"Sato 2531","created_at":"2025-05-20T13:31:48.458Z","published_at":"2025-10-27T11:07:13.533Z","updated_at":"2025-10-27T11:07:13.550Z","id":673915040,"uuid":"415b1d40-4220-45c8-9004-98c3acf8f73c","content":{"_uid":"a9af7d85-4805-4329-b71b-f5b2dea94b84","title":"Sato 2531","video":[{"_uid":"b30282d0-31ef-44ad-9a6e-daf72cee99f4","component":"video","vimeo_url":"","hosted_video":{"id":105972480866429,"alt":"SATO 2531 case film","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/x/cbba193727/250804_sato_logonashi.mp4","copyright":"","fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{"alt":"SATO 2531 case film","title":"","source":"","copyright":""},"is_external_url":false},"poster_image":{"id":22327764,"alt":"","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/1792x1008/2e6df4d121/sato-desktop.jpg","copyright":"","fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{},"is_external_url":false}}],"client":"Asuniwa","modules":[{"_uid":"f4e3290b-c8c4-4183-a2c2-c1a09fede804","quote":"Married couples in Japan are required to share a surname, predominantly affecting women and contributing to broader gender inequality. In partnership with Asuniwa, a gender equality organization, and the University of Tohoku, we revealed an eye-opening statistic to make a compelling case for reform.","credit":"","component":"quote_block","use_accent_color":true},{"_uid":"218fe07d-0ec5-481d-974c-9a15d53800ca","text":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":6},"content":[{"text":"Challenge ","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4},"content":[{"text":"ADDRESSING AN ENTRENCHED TRADITION TO IMPROVE EQUALITY","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"The law requiring married couples to share a surname in Japan has led to 95% of women changing their names. This law is deeply frustrating for women who have worked hard to build their careers and identities and represents a broader struggle for gender equality in society. Marriage rates in Japan have plummeted to their lowest levels since the 1930s; described by some as a “marriage ice age”. In a culture where few couples have children or live together outside marriage, this contributes to a declining birth rate and an ageing population. ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#000000"}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Previous attempts to shift policy makers’ attitudes had failed, despite campaigners’ passion and frustration. Protests and legal challenges to the surname law have spanned 40 years, but with limited success. In 2021, the Minister for Women’s Empowerment and Gender Equality opposed changing the law, despite its societal impact.","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#000000"}}]}]}]},"component":"rich_text","use_accent_color":false},{"_uid":"94bed2bf-0074-402c-8c7b-198216f9e30e","image":{"id":22327835,"alt":"","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/1920x1080/17e497db3a/1-sato.jpg","copyright":"","fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{},"is_external_url":false},"caption":"","component":"image_block","layout_size":"full-width","use_accent_color":false,"no_inner_parallax":true},{"_uid":"9924e614-2ec5-43e1-abc0-42c77fa02b15","image":{"id":22327846,"alt":"","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/2972x1672/69919cbdb0/2-sato.jpg","copyright":"","fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{},"is_external_url":false},"caption":"","component":"image_block","layout_size":"small","use_accent_color":false,"no_inner_parallax":true},{"_uid":"ec7a56dc-9f33-4949-ac74-55efb89a8d1b","text":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":6},"content":[{"text":"Approach ","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4},"content":[{"text":"Utilizing data to reframe the issue ","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"We needed a radically different approach to help our target see the problem in a new light. Instead of appealing to emotion, or a sense of injustice, we used data to reframe the issue; showing that the law was not only unfair but impractical. Not a women’s issue, but an issue affecting every individual, and the health of the nation itself. ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#000000"}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"We partnered with Professor Yoshida, Head of the Research Centre for Aged Economy and Society from Tohoku University to project the law's future impact. \"Sato\" is the most common surname in Japan, like Smith in the US, with 1.5% of the population sharing the name. Analyzing historical growth rates, Professor Yoshida projected the future dominance of the name, factoring in birth rates and population decline. We unearthed an extraordinary truth: without change, by 2531, everyone in Japan would be called “Sato”.","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#000000"}}]}]}]},"component":"rich_text","use_accent_color":false},{"_uid":"f119f72e-9df9-4d38-b51f-dc6c85e92891","image":{"id":22327927,"alt":"","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/2972x1672/8d0b80b16e/3-sato.jpg","copyright":"","fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{},"is_external_url":false},"caption":"","component":"image_block","layout_size":"large","use_accent_color":false,"no_inner_parallax":true},{"_uid":"31e9a2a3-e2e5-4538-902d-4926be50c864","image":{"id":22327932,"alt":"","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/2972x1672/c4f73ef6c7/4-sato.jpg","copyright":"","fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{},"is_external_url":false},"caption":"","component":"image_block","layout_size":"large","use_accent_color":false,"no_inner_parallax":true},{"_uid":"7e38e2c0-4f03-4318-ab28-8cbe9eba0cfb","text":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":6},"content":[{"text":"Solution ","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4},"content":[{"text":"A creative solution to demonstrate wider social impact","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"We knew that the data alone wasn't enough. We persuaded 40 companies to join with us to show the world what Japan 2531 would look like. Companies changed their logos and packaging to \"Sato,\" popular musicians, such as AI Kawashima, adopted the name \"Sato\", and sports team, Tokyo BB, switched their uniforms to name every player \"Sato.\" ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#000000"}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"This sparked consumers’ curiosity, who wondered, \"Why has my favorite brand become 'Sato'?\" We directed them to a website where we explained how Japan's marriage system is leading to the extinction of surnames. We also presented our findings to the UN Committee on the Elimination of Discrimination against Women. ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#000000"}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"The campaign, “Sato 2531,” generated a wave of coverage and conversation, reaching over 102 countries, delivering over 330m impressions and sparking a dramatic shift in attitudes and beliefs. Armed with the data, and a wave of public momentum, the Asuniwa organisation shared the findings of the survey with the UN Committee on the Elimination of Discrimination against Women, leading the UN to recommend that Japan revise the law within two years. ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#000000"}}]}]}]},"component":"rich_text","use_accent_color":false},{"_uid":"e266b30d-19e3-459e-baaf-fdd3fca23c38","image":{"id":22327967,"alt":"","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/2972x1672/141f683b8e/5-sato.jpg","copyright":"","fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{},"is_external_url":false},"caption":"","component":"image_block","layout_size":"large","use_accent_color":false,"no_inner_parallax":true},{"_uid":"0142c084-c9cb-4b1b-ba71-c4b136ff2feb","image":{"id":22327976,"alt":"","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/2972x1672/37911716a7/6-sato.jpg","copyright":"","fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{},"is_external_url":false},"caption":"","component":"image_block","layout_size":"small","use_accent_color":false,"no_inner_parallax":true},{"_uid":"faab797d-57b8-4d4c-9eab-38c226e5c48f","values":[{"_uid":"10200dd5-5a95-4ddb-93b2-395f37c48bac","number":"102","component":"statistic","unit_left":"","unit_right":"","description":"Countries covered the work, generating over 330 million impressions"},{"_uid":"cd08a521-a2fe-43b2-9b95-f8d72937234e","number":"78","component":"statistic","unit_left":"","unit_right":"%","description":"Of local government heads supported changing the law"},{"_uid":"026a232c-3f28-41bf-b61a-785d3f015276","number":"73","component":"statistic","unit_left":"","unit_right":"%","description":"Public support for changing the law has reached a record-breaking 73%"},{"_uid":"f26dbf76-9b06-4904-84aa-f409cdf94c7b","number":"2","component":"statistic","unit_left":"","unit_right":"","description":"The UN recommended Japan revise the law within two years"}],"component":"statistics","use_accent_color":false}],"category":["Changes society"],"component":"case","countries":[],"key_image":[{"_uid":"c499194b-d4f4-4911-be9d-6add99a0a62f","alt_text":"","component":"responsive_image","image_caption":"","image_portrait":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/1125x1800/9ba78a73fe/sato-mobile.jpg","image_landscape":"https://a.storyblok.com/f/155984/1792x1008/2e6df4d121/sato-desktop.jpg"}],"locations":[{"name":"Japan","created_at":"2024-04-25T14:59:13.583Z","published_at":"2026-03-27T12:12:41.021Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T12:12:41.035Z","id":485004737,"uuid":"a1a288df-75ec-405a-9e6c-35eeb17d99aa","content":{"_uid":"7ddf678f-3b2c-49a8-a704-3ac90945936b","city":"São Paulo","t